{
  "id": "22186_tayorinisuru",
  "headword": "{頼|たよ}りにする",
  "reading": "たよりにする",
  "romaji": "tayorinisuru",
  "part_of_speech": "expression, verb-suru",
  "gloss": "to rely on; to depend on; to count on",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to rely on; to depend on; to count on",
      "explanation": "To trust and depend on someone or something for help, support, or guidance. Implies confidence that the person or thing is reliable."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22186_tayorinisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "いつも{頼|たよ}りにしています。",
      "english": "I always count on you.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22186_tayorinisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{頼|たよ}りにできる{人|ひと}だ。",
      "english": "He's someone you can rely on.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22186_tayorinisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{困|こま}ったときにいつも{頼|たよ}りにしている{友人|ゆうじん}がいるのは{心強|こころづよ}い。",
      "english": "It's reassuring to have a friend I can always rely on when I'm in trouble.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A very common and warm expression used to tell someone you depend on them. Often used as a compliment. The ている form {頼|たよ}りにしている expresses an ongoing state of reliance.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～を{頼|たよ}りにする — to rely on ~\n- {頼|たよ}りにしています — I'm counting on you (polite; often said to colleagues or superiors)\n- {頼|たよ}りにできる — reliable, dependable\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {頼|たよ}る — to rely on; the basic verb, slightly more about depending as a need\n- {当|あ}てにする — to count on, expect; can imply an unreliable expectation\n- {信頼|しんらい}する — to trust; more formal, emphasizes deep trust",
